# Auth, webhooks, object access

## Identity

- Public **sign-up** off by default (`disableSignUp` / equivalent). Users created by admin only.
- Default role = **least privilege**, never `manager`/`admin` for self-serve signup.
- Separate apps = separate IdPs unless SSO is designed — do not assume shared `userId`/roles.
- UI hiding buttons ≠ authorization. Every mutation/read by id checks session + role + **object access** (no IDOR by swapping id).

## Ingest / webhooks

- Verify shared secret (prefer `timingSafeEqual`).
- Also enforce **resource ACL** (e.g. Telegram `chat.id` allowlist, tenant id) — secret alone is not enough if the bot is reachable from other chats.
- Retries must be idempotent; do not create duplicate orders on Telegram/webhook redelivery.

## Secrets & audit

- Never put API keys / ingest secrets in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`, client bundles, or committed real values.
- Audit (who/when/before/after) for: role changes, prices, discounts, status, warehouse write-offs, exports.

```text
❌ Webhook: if (secret OK) createOrder(payload)
✅ if (secret OK && chatId === ALLOWED) createOrder(idempotent)
```
